
"smart_sources:Lore for Flora's Regency Era (UPDATED)/meta/Contextual Rules 1.md": {"path":"Lore for Flora's Regency Era (UPDATED)/meta/Contextual Rules 1.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"1kgiwc9","at":1777331817895},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1776992716856,"size":2814,"at":1777331817922,"hash":"1kgiwc9"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,14],"#Contextual Rules 1":[16,32],"#Contextual Rules 1#{1}":[18,32]},"outlinks":[],"metadata":{"type":"lore","status":"active","priority":120,"tags":["#lorebook","#lorebook-always"],"position":"after","depth":4,"scanDepth":1,"summary":"**What this is:** A set of three fundamental worldbuilding rules defining the setting's physical and technological boundaries: (1) No magic or supernatural forces exist; (2) Gunpowder is extremely rare, limited to siege weapons and naval cannons; (3) Technology is 18th-century analogue (no electricity, no telegraph, no personal firearms).\n\n**When to select:** Whenever the narrative references supernatural events, personal firearms, gunpowder usage, advanced technology, or communication methods beyond handwritten letters. Also select when characters express belief in miracles, curses, or divine visions to ground them as superstition rather than reality.\n\n**Key relationships:** Directly contradicts any supernatural explanations. Governs the rarity of gunpowder (Contextual Rules 2, if exists). Establishes backdrop for Claymore Manor's mill-powered water pump as an exceptional advancement."},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},"smart_blocks:Lore for Flora's Regency Era (UPDATED)/meta/Contextual Rules 1.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"11ymvl8","at":1777331817895},"key":"Lore for Flora's Regency Era (UPDATED)/meta/Contextual Rules 1.md#---frontmatter---","lines":[1,14],"size":1065,"outlinks":[],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
